    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `extract_tables.py` file that extracts table cells and row structure from a document using a concrete external provider, I will choose Amazon Textract as the provider. Amazon Textract is a service that automatically extracts text and data from scanned documents. It is identifiable by the use of the `boto3` library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, and the specific service client `textract`. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789889414815,
          "start": 1789889411658
        },
        "type": "text"
